==Dialogue==
{{Stub Dialogue}}
:{{Black Screen|Concurrently, at the other end of the Luofu...}}
:'''Sushang:''' Hey, Luocha, you didn't finish telling us about the {{Rubi|Propagation|Aeon}}! Keep going &mdash; it's interesting. So Aeons can die, huh? Weird, I thought THEY were invincible...
:'''Luocha:''' There is no true invincibility or immortality in the world &mdash; such exaggerations are born of the perspectives of ordinary beings. Nonetheless, ordinary beings could not have orchestrated the fall of the Propagation... That Aeon was slain at the hands of another Aeon.
:'''Sushang:''' ...I don't understand. They're all Aeons, why do they want to fight?
:'''Luocha:''' You... Are you really from the Xianzhou!? Other Aeons aside, surely you must know the story of Lan and Yaoshi? Isn't destroying the Aeon Yaoshi the Alliance's cherished aim?
:'''Sushang:''' Of course, I know! Well, I know a little. My mum made me practice with swords all day &mdash; I didn't really go to school...
:'''Luocha:''' In that case... let's just change the subject. If you don't know about the feud between The Hunt and the Abundance, I'm afraid there's just too much to explain.
:'''Sushang:''' Fine, how's this for a subject &mdash; what's in the box?
:'''Luocha:''' Oh... this one? It's a casket, more commonly known as a coffin. It's for containing the remains of the deceased.
:'''Sushang:''' The deceased... A&mdash;Aren't you a merchant?
:'''Luocha:''' Yes indeed, this is just part of my job. I was asked to deliver this coffin to the Xianzhou. Ah, I'd quite forgotten &mdash; for long-life species, death is probably a distant concept?
:'''Sushang:''' Nope. The Cloud Knights spend a lot of time on the battlefield &mdash; death is a common occurrence. It's just, we don't put bodies in boxes &mdash; uh &mdash; coffins... In Xianzhou, people go to the Hall of Karma in the {{Rubi|Ten-Lords Commission|Long-Life Supervisory Authority}} and consecrate the names and jade abacuses of the dead. It's our way of saying goodbye.
:'''Sushang:''' The foxians and the Vidyadhara have their own ceremonies. Foxian soldiers place their dead in Starskiffs and then let them drift out into the stars. They call it "the Verdantia Returning."
:'''Sushang:''' As for the Vidyadhara, they're... more mysterious. They say that when a Vidyadhara is very old or has a fatal injury, they turn into an egg that looks like a pearl. When the shell breaks, they come out looking young again...
:'''Sushang:''' My mum calls the Vidyadhara "Long's Scions." When I was young, she told me stories of how the Vidyadhara could turn into dragons. I don't know if that's true...
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} It's true.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Only special Vidyadhara can turn into dragons.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} It's just a legend.
:'''Sushang:''' What do you know? Silent but deadly speaks.
:{{tx}}
{{Dialogue End}}

